  "emailSequences": {
    "lead-john-01": {
      "id": "seq-lead-john-01",
      "lead_id": "lead-john-01",
      "contact_name": "John Ishmael",
      "contact_email": "unavailable",
      "company_name": "Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe",
      "emails": [
        {
          "sequence_step": 1,
          "day_offset": 1,
          "step_title": "Initial Personalized Introduction",
          "subject": "Operations & multi-day journey orchestration at Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe",
          "body": "Hi John,\n\nNoticed Taziki's ongoing expansion across ~100 locations and your operational initiative connecting frontline guest feedback with multi-unit consistency.\n\nGiven your role as Chief Operating Officer overseeing operational standards across Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe's 100 locations, I wanted to share how multi-unit operators orchestrate complex customer journeys.\n\nAt OSVI.ai, we developed Journey — an orchestration layer above traditional voice and chat bots designed for multi-agent teamwork and outcome-driven automation. Rather than deploying isolated point solutions that hit dead-ends when an inquiry requires store intervention, Journey coordinates specialized long-horizon agents with persistent memory across channels and days, backed by strict guardrails and seamless human handoff.\n\nAre you open to a brief conversation next week to see how Journey approaches multi-day customer interaction orchestration across multi-unit operators?\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Amay Mishra / GTM Lead at OSVI.ai]\namaymishra1104@gmail.com\n\n---\nOpt-out: If this isn't relevant to your current operational priorities, reply 'unsubscribe' and I will immediately remove you from future notes.",
          "personalization_lines": [
            "Noticed Taziki's ongoing expansion across ~100 locations and your operational initiative connecting frontline guest feedback with multi-unit consistency.",
            "Given your role as Chief Operating Officer overseeing operational standards across Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe's 100 locations, I wanted to share how multi-unit operators orchestrate complex customer journeys."
          ],
          "evidence_references": [
            "~100 operating units across 16 states and COO appointment documented at tazikisfranchising.com.",
            "Sourced scale profile (100 locations) via https://www.tazikisfranchising.com/updates/introducing-tazikis-new-coo-john-ishmael"
          ],
          "evidence_ids": [
            "ev-tazikis-01",
            "ev-tazikis-02"
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_step": 2,
          "day_offset": 4,
          "step_title": "Relevant Use Case & Business Value",
          "subject": "Multi-day journey orchestration (proof from Domino's India)",
          "body": "Hi John,\n\nFollowing up on my earlier note.\n\nIn reviewing Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe's operations, we often observe that coordinating high-volume catering inquiries and store-level feedback across ~100 locations without overloading general managers. creates coordination strain between customer channels and store general managers.\n\nWhen standalone chatbots or automated phone menus handle inquiries, they typically lack persistent state. If a customer starts an interaction on mobile and follows up by phone two days later, context is lost.\n\nOSVI.ai Journey solves this by functioning as an orchestration layer above conversational bots:\n- Proven at Scale: In Domino's India's large-scale rider reactivation and recruitment journeys across WhatsApp and voice (supporting 7 languages for 100k+ riders), Journey achieved a 3x increase in chat conversions (case study: https://www.osvi.ai/case-studies/dominos).\n- Multi-Day Memory: Agents maintain persistent conversational context across multiple days for catering inquiries, crew onboarding, and guest feedback loops.\n- Deterministic Guardrails: Safely escalates operational exceptions directly to store managers with complete interaction history.\n\nWould you be open to a 10-minute walkthrough of how our multi-agent architecture coordinates complex workflows?\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Amay Mishra / GTM Lead at OSVI.ai]\namaymishra1104@gmail.com\n\n---\nOpt-out: Reply 'unsubscribe' to stop future emails.",
          "personalization_lines": [
            "In reviewing Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe's operations, we often observe that coordinating high-volume catering inquiries and store-level feedback across ~100 locations without overloading general managers. creates coordination strain between customer channels and store general managers."
          ],
          "evidence_references": [
            "Operational challenge assessment: Coordinating high-volume catering inquiries and store-level feedback across ~100 locations without overloading general managers."
          ],
          "evidence_ids": [
            "ev-tazikis-01"
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_step": 3,
          "day_offset": 8,
          "step_title": "Thoughtful Workflow Question",
          "subject": "Question on Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe's multi-day inquiry handoffs",
          "body": "Hi John,\n\nAs Chief Operating Officer managing operational execution across 100 locations, you know where single-turn AI chatbots hit limits.\n\nI had a quick question regarding how your team currently handles multi-touchpoint interactions:\n\nWhen a customer inquiry spans multiple days — such as a large catering reservation change, a driver onboarding question, or an escalated guest service loop — how do your current systems coordinate that request between front-line channels and store teams?\n\nMost operators tell us their bots either drop the ball or blindly forward unstructured emails to store managers. Journey was built to orchestrate long-horizon teamwork among autonomous agents so customer inquiries reach actual operational resolution.\n\nCurious if this is an area you are exploring this quarter.\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Amay Mishra / GTM Lead at OSVI.ai]\namaymishra1104@gmail.com\n\n---\nOpt-out: Reply 'unsubscribe' to stop future emails.",
          "personalization_lines": [
            "As Chief Operating Officer managing operational execution across 100 locations, you know where single-turn AI chatbots hit limits."
          ],
          "evidence_references": [
            "Role inquiry for Chief Operating Officer (100 locations)"
          ],
          "evidence_ids": [
            "ev-tazikis-01"
          ]
        },
        {
          "sequence_step": 4,
          "day_offset": 13,
          "step_title": "Polite Close-the-Loop Message",
          "subject": "Closing the loop — OSVI Journey & Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe",
          "body": "Hi John,\n\nI recognize you're fully focused on driving operational performance across Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe's 100 locations. I don't want to crowd your inbox if multi-agent journey orchestration is not a current priority.\n\nIf you ever explore ways to move beyond traditional standalone bots toward long-horizon agent teamwork with persistent memory, guardrails, and safe human handoff, feel free to reach back out.\n\nWishing you and the Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe team continued operational success.\n\nWarm regards,\n\n[Amay Mishra / GTM Lead at OSVI.ai]\namaymishra1104@gmail.com\n\n---\nOpt-out: Reply 'unsubscribe' to stop future emails.",
          "personalization_lines": [
            "I recognize you're fully focused on driving operational performance across Taziki's Mediterranean Cafe's 100 locations."
          ],
          "evidence_references": [
            "Summary closing referencing 100 locations"
          ],
          "evidence_ids": [
            "ev-tazikis-01"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "status": "GENERATED",
      "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:28:58.292Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-23T20:46:53.734Z"
    }
  },
